// What someone's job is, as distinct from whether they own the account.
//
// Part of the multi-file Prisma schema in this folder.
//
// UserRole is deliberately NOT touched. It has exactly two values and
// answers exactly one question — can this person administer the company
// (invite, remove, delete, connect integrations). Every assertOwner() call
// site in lib/actions/* means that and keeps meaning it. Folding
// "estimator" and "foreman" into the same enum would have made every one
// of those guards ambiguous overnight, and a permissions guard that means
// two things is a security bug waiting for its first Monday.
//
// So this is a second, orthogonal column. Ownership says who administers;
// job function says what the person does, and what they therefore need to
// see. The two compose: an OWNER always has every capability regardless of
// job function, because an owner locked out of their own books by a
// dropdown is a support call nobody can resolve from inside the app.

/// The jobs people actually hold at a specialty subcontractor, which is
/// not the same list as a generic CRM's.
///
/// NULL is a real and important value: it means nobody has said, and the
/// person keeps exactly the access every MEMBER has had until now — full
/// office access below owner-only administration. That is what makes this
/// migration safe on a company already using the app. There is no backfill
/// guess here; guessing that the quiet member is a foreman would silently
/// take the books away from a bookkeeper.
enum JobFunction {
  /// Runs the business. Same capabilities as an owner, without the
  /// account administration — a partner or a general manager.
  EXECUTIVE
  /// Prices work. Estimating, the catalog, bids, vendor pricing.
  ESTIMATOR
  /// Runs jobs. Everything operational plus job cost, which is how a PM
  /// knows whether the job is working.
  PROJECT_MANAGER
  /// Foreman or field lead. Jobs, field reports, safety, punch lists,
  /// time — and deliberately NOT margin, cost, billing or company
  /// financials. This is the tier the audit calls "field-only access",
  /// and it is the only one that removes anything.
  FIELD
  /// Certified payroll, union fringe, licences, insurance, bonds.
  PAYROLL_COMPLIANCE
  /// Invoices, pay applications, retainage, backcharges, the accounting
  /// sync.
  ACCOUNTING
}
